{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quicksort pivot quicksort pivot","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md","fileName":"Quicksort Pivot.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quicksort Pivot","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Sorting Algorithms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sorting Algorithms","Quicksort","algorithms.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quicksort pivot quicksort pivot","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md","fileName":"Quicksort Pivot.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quicksort Pivot","heading":"Quicksort Pivot","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A quicksort pivot is the item used to partition a collection during [[Quicksort]]. Items smaller than the pivot move to one side, while items at least as large move to the other, leaving the pivot in its final sorted position.\n\nAn extreme pivot such as the current minimum produces a badly unbalanced partition and little progress. Selecting pivots at random avoids spending extra work searching for an ideal pivot while making a long sequence of worst choices exceedingly improbable.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sorting Algorithms","Quicksort","algorithms.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quicksort pivot quicksort pivot","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quicksort Pivot.md","fileName":"Quicksort Pivot.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title"